        "title": "The California Building",
        "body": "Unlike the other state buildings, the California Building did not house exhibits for the state's various industries (that job being left to the individual county buildings) but instead acted as a gathering place and headquarters for those running the exposition. Additionally, it had some exhibits of Mexico and Central American Native peoples, as they were deemed \"another Egypt\". The building was intended to be permanent and today houses the Museum of Us.",
